    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver. The $4.50 cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-02713 is refunded to the rider in full, and the platform will pay the driver a $2.25 goodwill payment (50% of that fee). The two figures are independent and are never netted against each other, and the $2.25 comes from the platform, not from the rider. They total $6.75.\n\nWhere the driver actually was. The driver's GPS trace carries 73 fixes and never places him inside the 120 m arrival radius for this LARGE_VENUE pickup: 0 qualifying in-radius fixes, closest approach 227.26 m from the pin, longest qualifying run 0.0 s. Under POL-NS-02 he therefore did not 'arrive' at the pickup point, POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails, and the fee is not chargeable and is refunded in full (POL-NS-02; also POL-NS-06, effective in-geofence dwell 0 s against the 180 s free period read from trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec). The rider's claims to that effect are accepted.\n\nWhy the driver is still owed something. The same trace shows him stationary at 227.26 m from the pin, marking 'I'm Here' at 07:35:42, the wait timer starting at 07:35:44, and the cancellation at 07:41:12 - a 330-second hold, longer than the 180-second free period. A stationary position outside the 120 m radius but within 400 m is the POL-NS-03 case, and POL-NS-02 expressly yields to POL-NS-03 'including the driver's compensation'. The driver's mean distance of 1,547.34 m and top speed of 62.7 km/h describe his 5.7 km approach to the venue, not the wait, so the rider's argument built on those two figures does not displace POL-NS-03.\n\nWhich POL-NS-03 limb. Neither party named an entrance, block, tower or bay: the driver wrote only 'im here' and 'im here already, where are you', the rider only 'cant see you'. trip_record.registered_pickup_points is 3. Limb (i) therefore does not apply and limb (ii) does: the mislocation is pin ambiguity rather than fault, and the platform-funded goodwill is 50% x $4.50 = $2.25. The two points are not treated as the same bay on general knowledge; the 227.26 m distance is what decides it.\n\nOn the money figures contested between the parties. The $3.60 shown in the fare ledger's derived money block is NOT paid: POL-NS-07 compensates only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and it is not, so the rider is right that no fee-funded payout arises. That does not reach the POL-NS-03(ii) goodwill, which is platform-funded. No false-arrival referral arises either: the arrival marker in force is BUTTON (so POL-NS-12 does not apply), and at 07:35:42 the driver was within 300 m of the pin and stationary, so POL-NS-05 is not triggered and its referral does not fire.\n\nNo escalation. Confidence is 0.85, above the 0.70 floor. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check is not tripped (no_show_terminations_30d 1, below 4; 1/60 = 0.017, below 0.08), rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1 (below the 3 POL-NS-09 reads), and neither profile shows 90-day counterparty disputes. No artifact the ruling rests on is impaired under POL-NS-08(a)-(d): the trace, trip record, chat log and fare breakdown are all COMPLETE at weight 1.0. The absent traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02713-01 (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact and only closes POL-NS-06(i)'s accumulation route. The monetary effect, $4.50 + $2.25 = $6.75, is below the $8.00 execution threshold, so this ruling executes automatically."
