    "explanation": "Both of you: the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee is refunded to the rider in full, and the driver is paid a platform-funded goodwill of SGD 2.25. Both figures are read off the money block (fare_breakdown fee_charged 4.50; derived goodwill 2.25).\n\nWHY THE FEE IS REFUNDED. In this category arrival and dwell are measured from the GPS trace, not from the 'I'm Here' tap. POL-NS-02 deems a driver arrived only where the trace holds at least three consecutive fixes inside the arrival radius — 120 m for a LARGE_VENUE pickup such as Tampines Mall. Across the whole attempt the driver's 73 fixes never came closer than 227.26 m to the pin, so there are no qualifying in-radius fixes, POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails, and the rider is entitled to a full refund. The 'I'm Here' event at 07:35:42 and the 180 s wait timer started at 07:35:44 do not change that: the arrival marker in force is BUTTON, and POL-NS-12 gives a driver-pressed marker no independent carrier status, so the proximity test governs. The effective in-geofence dwell is 0 s against the 180 s free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec), a 180.0 s shortfall under POL-NS-06. The rider's own track places the rider at the pin throughout — 70 of 70 qualifying fixes between 16.06 m and 23.13 m of the pickup, all at 0 km/h — and the ledger line is refunded in full (refund_issued_sgd 0.00 presently).\n\nWHY THIS IS A WRONG-ENTRANCE CASE (the rider's POL-NS-02 point, accepted in part). The driver's closest approach, 227.26 m, is outside the 120 m arrival radius but well inside the 400 m ceiling of POL-NS-03, and the trace shows him holding there through the waiting window (about 330 s, from the 07:35:42 arrival tap to the 07:41:12 cancellation). POL-NS-02 states that where the driver was stationary for the required dwell within 400 m of the pin, POL-NS-03 governs the outcome including the driver's compensation, and POL-NS-02 yields to it. That is this case, so the POL-NS-06 shortfall arithmetic the rider relies on sets the refund but is displaced on the allocation of cost. I do not accept the rider's point that the driver's whole-trace average distance of 1,547 m shows he was never near the venue: that average is dominated by his 5.73 km approach, and the operative fact is his closest position, 227.26 m. POL-NS-05 is not engaged — at the arrival instant the trace places him at 227.26 m, inside its 300 m distance threshold — so no false-arrival referral arises, and the MISSING advisory (EV-ADVIS-02713-01) is immaterial because there is no second in-geofence interval for POL-NS-06(i) to accumulate.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S PAYMENT. Under POL-NS-03 fault is allocated from the chat log. Neither party named an entrance, block, tower or bay — the driver wrote only 'im here' and 'im here already, where are you', the rider only 'cant see you' — and trip_record.registered_pickup_points is 3, i.e. 2 or more. Under POL-NS-03(ii) the mislocation is therefore attributed to pin ambiguity rather than to either party, and the driver receives a platform-funded goodwill of 50 percent of the cancellation fee in force: 0.50 x SGD 4.50 = SGD 2.25, charged to the platform and never recovered from the rider. This is not the SGD 3.60 the fare ledger shows for POL-NS-07: POL-NS-07 compensates only a driver whose POL-NS-01 conditions all hold, and limb (b) does not (the rider's no-compensation point is accepted as to the 3.60). POL-NS-06's sentence that no driver compensation is payable speaks to that fee-funded payout, not to POL-NS-03(ii)'s platform-funded goodwill. Under POL-GEN-03 the rider's refund and the driver's goodwill are independent and are never netted; the ruling value names the filing party's outcome, FULL_REFUND, with amount_sgd 4.50 and driver_compensation_sgd 2.25.\n\nPOL-NS-04 (the driver's point, accepted). POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider and strip the driver: the driver replied to the rider's 07:37:22 message at 07:38:12, 50 s later and within the 120 s window limb (b) sets, and the clause states that where the driver did reply within 120 s it does not apply regardless of the reply's content. No in-app call was needed and none was made.\n\nESCALATION AND REFERRALS (both sides' points, accepted). No trigger fires. My confidence (0.85) is above the 0.70 floor. The trip record's arrival tap and the GPS trace are reconciled by POL-NS-01(c), POL-NS-05 and POL-NS-12 rather than left in open conflict, so POL-NS-09(b) is not engaged. Both disputes_with_counterparty_90d counters are 0. rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below the 3 POL-NS-09(d) reads. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d = 1 is below 4 and 1/60 = 0.017 is below 0.08. No clause directs a referral on these facts, so none is recorded. The monetary effect is SGD 6.75 (4.50 + 2.25), below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically on issue. This ruling is provisional; either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04.",
